~ start
# Scene: A raised podium in the central square of Levaris. Two soldiers stand at attention beside it, mid-announcement to a gathered crowd. Astryn, Novius, Spero, and Aegrandir stand among the townsfolk.

do cutscene.wait_before_dialogue()

solider_one: —and remember, curfew violations will be handled swiftly and without exception. General Vorkoth's justice is Levaris's peace.

solider_one: Any further business brought before this podium will be heard now, as is custom.

solider_two: You four. You're not from here.

astryn: Observant.

solider_two: State your business in Levaris.

astryn: We're here to speak with Vorkoth.

solider_one: The General does not entertain outsiders on a whim. Move along.

spero: Didn't you just say any business gets heard? Or was that just for show?

solider_two: Watch your tone, boy.

do vorkoth.play_teleport_in()

do AudioController.play_background_music()

vorkoth_p1: Now, now. No need to rattle our guests.

spero: DAMN, that hairline is nasty...

astryn: Not now.

vorkoth_p1: ...Something funny, boy?

spero: Nope. Just admiring the view.

vorkoth_p1: Word travels fast when strangers cause a scene in my city. What is it you want with me?

novius: We traced a medicine distributor here. Every inflated price, every backroom deal — leads straight back to a cut you're taking off the top.

vorkoth_p1: And you'd be the expert on medicine, would you?

novius: I used to work the counter myself. I know exactly what a price tag like that does to somebody who can't pay it.

vorkoth_p1: Touching. Truly. But accusations aren't proof, boy.

astryn: We've got enough of both. We're not asking.

vorkoth_p1: And you're the one bringing me this? Leading these three?

astryn: I am.

vorkoth_p1: Huh. Do you have any idea what I've built here? The order I've kept? And you show up spouting rumors like you know the first thing about running a city.

vorkoth_p1: I'll tell you what I think is really going on. I think you're jealous. I think you saw a strong city, a strong leader, and you couldn't stand it — so you came to tear it down instead of building something of your own.

novius: That's not an answer. It's a dodge.

vorkoth_p1: It wasn't meant for you, either.

astryn: (to the party) He's not gonna give us anything straight. Figured as much.

astryn: (to Vorkoth) Fine. Then we'll settle it the old-fashioned way. I challenge you to a duel, Vorkoth. You lose, you step down as general of Levaris. Publicly. Tonight.

# The crowd goes silent. Soldiers exchange uneasy glances.

solider_one: That's outrageous! You don't get to challenge a general of Acirema like some tavern brawl—

vorkoth_p1: You. A duel. With me.

astryn: Something funny?

vorkoth_p1: I've put down warlords twice your size and half your mouth. I'm trying to imagine what exactly you think you bring to a duel that they didn't.

astryn: Guess you'll find out tonight.

vorkoth_p1: (to the crowd) You hear this? A girl walks into my city and thinks she's the one to end my rule!

vorkoth_p1: (back to Astryn) Very well. I accept — if only to remind this city, and the rest of Acirema, what happens to those who overestimate themselves.

vorkoth_p1: Tonight. The Pit. Try not to embarrass yourself.

do vorkoth.play_teleport_out()

# Vorkoth vanishes as suddenly as he appeared. The soldiers usher the crowd along. The party is left standing in the square.

astryn: Let's use the time we've got. Talk around the city. I want to know exactly what we're walking into tonight.

=> END
